1
00:00:02,580 --> 00:00:04,960
Only three days left till the new year.

2
00:00:05,420 --> 00:00:08,008
And I hope you're all
enjoying your holiday.

3
00:00:08,700 --> 00:00:10,860
Hey, were you up late again?

4
00:00:11,400 --> 00:00:15,280
Yeah, for a mechatronics
project for school. Mecha-what?

5
00:00:15,660 --> 00:00:16,680
Sounds fun.

6
00:00:19,400 --> 00:00:21,240
Kazuto, you see this yet?

7
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:22,937
What the?!

8
00:00:23,020 --> 00:00:26,037
The Holy Sword Excalibur
has been found in ALO?!

9
00:00:26,120 --> 00:00:28,120
Oh man, that sucks.

10
00:00:28,440 --> 00:00:30,969
I can't believe someone
else beat us to it.

11
00:00:31,280 --> 00:00:32,751
Read the article, Doofus.

12
00:00:32,920 --> 00:00:34,357
It says it's been found is all.

13
00:00:34,440 --> 00:00:36,146
No one's actually got it yet.

14
00:00:38,300 --> 00:00:39,460
Yeah, you're right.

15
00:00:39,640 --> 00:00:41,111
Don't scare me like that.

16
00:00:43,200 --> 00:00:45,700
A couple months ago on the Arun Plains,

17
00:00:46,140 --> 00:00:49,611
Leafa, Yui, and me got swallowed
by a big-ass monster worm.

18
00:00:49,760 --> 00:00:52,995
It dropped us in an underground
realm called Jotunheim.

19
00:00:53,340 --> 00:00:57,617
We looked around for a bit and came
across this four-armed humanoid monster.

20
00:00:57,700 --> 00:00:59,477
It was fighting another
monster that looked

21
00:00:59,560 --> 00:01:02,442
like a cross between an
elephant and a jellyfish.

22
00:01:02,640 --> 00:01:03,520
Go figure.

23
00:01:04,080 --> 00:01:07,317
Leafa felt sorry for the jellyphant
thing and told me to go save it.

24
00:01:07,400 --> 00:01:10,837
I lured forearms onto this frozen
lake and it fell through the ice.

25
00:01:10,920 --> 00:01:13,038
Then the jellyphant took care of it.

26
00:01:14,600 --> 00:01:16,424
Leafa decided to call it Tonki,

27
00:01:16,640 --> 00:01:20,557
and suddenly it transformed into an even
weirder-looking thing with eight wings.

28
00:01:20,640 --> 00:01:25,522
We hopped on its back and it took us to a
passageway, leading to the surface world.

29
00:01:28,700 --> 00:01:30,720
On the way up was when we saw it.

30
00:01:31,260 --> 00:01:35,025
An upside-down pyramid hanging
from the roots of the world tree.

31
00:01:35,440 --> 00:01:38,560
And a long golden sword shimmering inside.

32
00:01:45,420 --> 00:01:46,250
Excalibur.

33
00:01:47,380 --> 00:01:50,837
I was planning on going back
for it someday, but now...

34
00:01:50,920 --> 00:01:54,697
It'd be a nice break from all that
floor-clearing you're doing in New Aincrad.

35
00:01:54,780 --> 00:01:57,777
This article doesn't say
anything about how they found it.

36
00:01:57,860 --> 00:02:00,137
Players can't fly in Jotunheim, remember?

37
00:02:00,220 --> 00:02:02,337
But that's the only way to spot Excalibur.

38
00:02:02,420 --> 00:02:04,302
That thing's too high up to see.

39
00:02:04,720 --> 00:02:06,877
Unless they rescued
one of Tonki's friends,

40
00:02:06,960 --> 00:02:08,797
hitched a ride, and
triggered the quest flag.

41
00:02:08,880 --> 00:02:11,292
If we could do it, so could someone else.

42
00:02:11,400 --> 00:02:13,737
I guess that makes sense, although...

43
00:02:13,820 --> 00:02:15,500
Who'd trust a creepy...

44
00:02:17,660 --> 00:02:21,877
Uh, I mean, who'd trust such a unique
monster unless they had weird tape?

45
00:02:21,960 --> 00:02:24,240
I mean, a weirdly big heart.

46
00:02:25,380 --> 00:02:26,968
Someone just like you, sis.

47
00:02:27,100 --> 00:02:27,930
What are the odds?

48
00:02:28,013 --> 00:02:28,937
He's not creepy.

49
00:02:29,020 --> 00:02:29,850
He's adorable.

50
00:02:30,980 --> 00:02:34,077
Anyway, the whole point of showing
you that was to get you going.

51
00:02:34,160 --> 00:02:35,957
It's only a matter of time before someone

52
00:02:36,040 --> 00:02:38,417
grinds through that
dungeon and gets the sword.

53
00:02:38,500 --> 00:02:39,330
You're right.

54
00:02:39,560 --> 00:02:40,501
Clock's ticking.

55
00:02:41,180 --> 00:02:43,356
So what are you going to do about it?

56
00:02:47,060 --> 00:02:49,777
Sugu, getting rare items
isn't the point of it.

57
00:02:49,860 --> 00:02:52,577
If that's all you play
for, you're missing out.

58
00:02:52,660 --> 00:02:54,440
Yeah, I guess you're right.

59
00:02:54,660 --> 00:02:57,037
There's funner things to
do than boosting stats.

60
00:02:57,120 --> 00:02:58,179
I wasn't finished.

61
00:02:58,400 --> 00:03:02,457
I think Tonki wanted us to find it, and
that's why he showed us where it was.

62
00:03:02,540 --> 00:03:04,977
For some reason, he needs
us to clear that dungeon,

63
00:03:05,060 --> 00:03:07,648
so it's up to us to
make his wish come true.

64
00:03:08,360 --> 00:03:11,837
Tonki's our friend, and there's no
way I'm turning my back on a friend.

65
00:03:11,920 --> 00:03:12,750
Ooh.

66
00:03:13,200 --> 00:03:15,788
A minute ago, you called
your friend creepy.

67
00:03:17,780 --> 00:03:19,257
I meant creepy cool.

68
00:03:19,340 --> 00:03:20,260
Anyway, you in?

69
00:03:21,040 --> 00:03:21,870
Sure.

70
00:03:21,953 --> 00:03:23,857
I don't have practice
because of the holidays.

71
00:03:23,940 --> 00:03:24,770
Awesome!

72
00:03:24,880 --> 00:03:26,557
Okay, we'll need seven others.

73
00:03:26,640 --> 00:03:28,097
We don't want to overload Tonki.

74
00:03:28,180 --> 00:03:30,533
For starters, we got you, me, and Asuna.

75
00:03:30,760 --> 00:03:32,878
Then there's Klein, Liz, and Silica.

76
00:03:34,600 --> 00:03:36,277
We need one more person.

77
00:03:36,360 --> 00:03:38,007
Eggiel's gotta work tonight.

78
00:03:39,340 --> 00:03:40,777
Chris Height's not leveled up yet.

79
00:03:40,860 --> 00:03:42,777
Rekon's grinding in Sylph territory.

80
00:03:42,860 --> 00:03:43,860
Oh, I know!

81
00:03:44,100 --> 00:03:45,865
Let's ask Xenon to come along!

82
00:03:46,200 --> 00:03:48,820
Great idea, sis! What'd you expect?

83
00:03:49,140 --> 00:03:50,728
I'll message him right now.

84
00:03:50,860 --> 00:03:52,120
Except for Asuna.

85
00:03:52,300 --> 00:03:54,080
I'll leave that to you. Okay.

86
00:03:59,320 --> 00:04:03,240
I wish I could see Kirito again
before I go visit my grandparents.

87
00:04:09,440 --> 00:04:10,600
Hi, Kirito!

88
00:04:11,240 --> 00:04:12,160
Morning, Asuna.

89
00:04:12,600 --> 00:04:13,953
Sorry to call so early.

90
00:04:14,480 --> 00:04:17,951
We were planning on going on
a quest in ALO this afternoon.

91
00:04:18,040 --> 00:04:19,080
You want to go?

92
00:04:19,420 --> 00:04:20,714
Yeah, I'll totally go.

93
00:04:20,820 --> 00:04:22,037
I'm free all day today.

94
00:04:22,120 --> 00:04:22,950
Cool.

95
00:04:23,033 --> 00:04:26,057
I'll text you the time and
place, so keep an eye out for it.

96
00:04:26,140 --> 00:04:27,240
You know I will.

97
00:04:27,720 --> 00:04:29,602
See you in a little while, then.

98
00:04:31,080 --> 00:04:31,910
Yes!

99
00:04:43,320 --> 00:04:50,260
So, I'll never forget that
I'm a man who flew away. .

100
00:04:51,440 --> 00:04:53,117
I've been working for the
day that I've been doing,

101
00:04:53,200 --> 00:04:56,037
but I've been working for a long time.

102
00:04:56,120 --> 00:05:01,580
I'm not sure what's going on.

103
00:05:02,220 --> 00:05:03,050
I'm not sure what's going on.

104
00:05:03,133 --> 00:05:04,957
.

105
00:05:05,040 --> 00:05:06,500
.

106
00:05:08,100 --> 00:05:12,617
It's the end of the world.

107
00:05:12,700 --> 00:05:15,257
It's the end of the story.

108
00:05:15,340 --> 00:05:16,928
The story of the beginning.

109
00:05:18,380 --> 00:05:21,317
It's the end of the song.

110
00:05:21,400 --> 00:05:24,737
You can see the future.

111
00:05:24,820 --> 00:05:29,160
The world is the one who is in
the sky. It's been a long time.

112
00:05:31,420 --> 00:05:34,100
It's been a long time.

113
00:06:00,720 --> 00:06:02,600
Oh, give it for my way.

114
00:06:11,660 --> 00:06:14,895
Hey, Klein, do you get to
take vacation for New Year's?

115
00:06:15,200 --> 00:06:16,788
Been on it since yesterday.

116
00:06:17,100 --> 00:06:21,017
Even if I wanted to work and I don't,
there's no shipments this time of year.

117
00:06:21,100 --> 00:06:22,897
You know what my cheap-ass boss said?

118
00:06:22,980 --> 00:06:26,137
Be thankful you got a job where you
get a whole week off for New Year's,

119
00:06:26,220 --> 00:06:28,817
bragging about it like
he was doing us a favor.

120
00:06:28,900 --> 00:06:30,440
And speaking of favors,

121
00:06:30,660 --> 00:06:33,017
if we do manage to snag Excalibur today,

122
00:06:33,100 --> 00:06:37,806
How about doing me a solid and help me
get my hands on the Soul Blade Kaguzuchi?

123
00:06:38,640 --> 00:06:39,470
Seriously?

124
00:06:39,553 --> 00:06:41,337
That dungeon's like a freaking oven, man.

125
00:06:41,420 --> 00:06:43,337
Yeah, well, I'm going
to Jotunheim for you,

126
00:06:43,420 --> 00:06:45,477
where it's colder than
the ass end of an ice pop.

127
00:06:45,560 --> 00:06:48,148
You know, I want something
out of this, too.

128
00:06:48,580 --> 00:06:49,580
The Shekinah bow.

129
00:06:50,620 --> 00:06:55,137
Your avatar's two weeks old, and already
you're gunning for a legendary weapon?

130
00:06:55,220 --> 00:06:57,997
Yeah, well, that bow Liz
made me as great and all,

131
00:06:58,080 --> 00:07:00,397
but I need something
with a little more range.

132
00:07:00,480 --> 00:07:01,310
Oh, yeah?

133
00:07:01,393 --> 00:07:04,120
Then what the heck are you
using a bow and A .L .O. for?

134
00:07:04,420 --> 00:07:06,697
Their range falls between
the spears and magic.

135
00:07:06,780 --> 00:07:11,337
You're like the only player who wants to
use these things to snipe from 100 meters.

136
00:07:11,420 --> 00:07:14,620
If I had my way, I'd want
double that range at least.

137
00:07:18,420 --> 00:07:19,560
We're back, guys!

138
00:07:19,900 --> 00:07:21,018
Thanks for waiting.

139
00:07:21,260 --> 00:07:24,240
We thought you were never
coming back. What's up?

140
00:07:24,440 --> 00:07:25,969
You get lost or something?

141
00:07:26,100 --> 00:07:26,960
Not at all.

142
00:07:27,120 --> 00:07:29,517
We were gathering
information while we shopped.

143
00:07:29,600 --> 00:07:32,220
We talked to a whole
bunch of people, Daddy,

144
00:07:32,540 --> 00:07:36,305
and so far not one player or party
has reached that dungeon yet.

145
00:07:37,280 --> 00:07:38,110
Really?

146
00:07:38,193 --> 00:07:40,877
Well, then how the heck do
they know where Excalibur's at?

147
00:07:40,960 --> 00:07:42,372
That's the thing, Daddy.

148
00:07:42,460 --> 00:07:44,237
No one really knows where it is.

149
00:07:44,320 --> 00:07:47,497
Apparently they found a different
quest than the one Tonki showed us.

150
00:07:47,580 --> 00:07:51,345
They met an NPC who told them if
they finished this other quest,

151
00:07:51,440 --> 00:07:53,540
they'd get Excalibur as the reward.

152
00:07:54,460 --> 00:07:58,636
And from what we heard, the quest
they're going on isn't very pleasant.

153
00:07:59,260 --> 00:08:03,142
Instead of a delivery quest or an
escort quest, it's a kill quest.

154
00:08:03,480 --> 00:08:05,320
Just slaughtering monsters.

155
00:08:06,340 --> 00:08:10,117
Everyone in Jotunheim is out there
right now killing as many as they can.

156
00:08:10,200 --> 00:08:13,317
Yeah, that doesn't even sound
close to being pleasant.

157
00:08:13,400 --> 00:08:15,988
This whole thing sounds
sketchy to me, guys.

158
00:08:16,280 --> 00:08:17,456
Here's what we know.

159
00:08:17,660 --> 00:08:21,257
There's a dungeon in the sky with
Excalibur locked up at the bottom of it.

160
00:08:21,340 --> 00:08:23,977
To get to it, you gotta fight your
way through a bunch of monsters.

161
00:08:24,060 --> 00:08:27,717
But now we got an NPC offering
it up as a kill quest reward?

162
00:08:27,800 --> 00:08:31,440
That's bizarre now that you
mention it? That is weird!

163
00:08:32,380 --> 00:08:36,851
The NBC is not showing anyone to the
dungeon, but that's where the sword is.

164
00:08:38,880 --> 00:08:41,939
Well, I'm sure we'll find
out why once we get there!

165
00:08:44,040 --> 00:08:47,628
Alrighty, your weapons are all
restored and ready for action.

166
00:09:00,160 --> 00:09:02,177
Even though our party's full of hotness,

167
00:09:02,260 --> 00:09:04,557
we're still a bunch of
gear-toting meatheads.

168
00:09:04,640 --> 00:09:07,457
If you want to switch it up, you
could always boost your magic.

169
00:09:07,540 --> 00:09:09,060
Ha! Keep dreaming.

170
00:09:09,400 --> 00:09:10,277
A real samurai?

171
00:09:10,360 --> 00:09:12,800
He wouldn't be caught dead using magic.

172
00:09:12,960 --> 00:09:14,000
Code of Honor.

173
00:09:14,200 --> 00:09:15,420
Code of Honor, huh?

174
00:09:15,920 --> 00:09:18,557
Know what samurais are
classified as in RPGs?

175
00:09:18,640 --> 00:09:21,900
They're both warriors and
black magic users. Please.

176
00:09:22,200 --> 00:09:26,037
I'd rather bust my sword and quit
being a samurai than use magic, doll.

177
00:09:26,120 --> 00:09:27,137
I don't know, Klein.

178
00:09:27,220 --> 00:09:31,117
If I remember, Red, didn't you use
a flame sword skill the other day?

179
00:09:31,200 --> 00:09:34,197
You know, when you activate
it, you are using part magic.

180
00:09:34,280 --> 00:09:35,440
No way! Really?

181
00:09:35,860 --> 00:09:38,200
Yes, Klein, what Silica said is true.

182
00:09:38,920 --> 00:09:40,332
Remember the Mei update?

183
00:09:40,620 --> 00:09:43,679
It brought a whole bunch
of new sword skills to ALO.

184
00:09:44,060 --> 00:09:47,800
Some are physical and others
are advanced, like Earth, Water,

185
00:09:48,120 --> 00:09:52,560
Fire, Wind, Dark, and Divine, all
of which are magical attributes.

186
00:09:53,000 --> 00:09:54,840
Fire is magical too, huh?

187
00:09:55,500 --> 00:09:58,500
Okay, ex-samurai, you need
help busting that sword?

188
00:10:00,040 --> 00:10:01,960
Dude, back me up here.

189
00:10:02,460 --> 00:10:07,077
Well, since you don't chant when using
sword skills, I guess it's not the same.

190
00:10:07,160 --> 00:10:09,000
I'll let it slide this time.

191
00:10:12,680 --> 00:10:16,504
I really appreciate you guys
helping me out on such short notice.

192
00:10:17,800 --> 00:10:20,837
Seriously, you don't know
how much this means to me.

193
00:10:20,920 --> 00:10:23,640
Alright, are you ready? Yeah!

194
00:10:29,140 --> 00:10:29,970
God!

195
00:10:30,053 --> 00:10:32,208
How many steps does
this thing have, anyway?

196
00:10:33,540 --> 00:10:34,370
I know.

197
00:10:34,453 --> 00:10:36,637
I bet the tower on the
dungeon floor of New

198
00:10:36,720 --> 00:10:39,249
Ein Kirito doesn't even
have as many as this.

199
00:10:39,900 --> 00:10:40,920
Oh, come on.

200
00:10:41,140 --> 00:10:42,157
It's not that bad.

201
00:10:42,240 --> 00:10:45,797
If we took the normal route to
Jotunheim, it'd take at least two hours.

202
00:10:45,880 --> 00:10:47,821
This way, it's just five minutes.

203
00:10:48,100 --> 00:10:49,957
Instead of complaining about the steps,

204
00:10:50,040 --> 00:10:52,757
you should be thanking me for
showing you guys this rad shortcut.

205
00:10:52,840 --> 00:10:54,320
Yeah, yeah, you're right.

206
00:10:54,560 --> 00:10:55,897
It's still a pain in the butt.

207
00:10:55,980 --> 00:10:57,627
I got your pain in the butt.

208
00:11:00,820 --> 00:11:01,700
Why, you!

209
00:11:04,400 --> 00:11:08,282
Dumbass, do that again, and you
get a fire arrow in your pie hole!

210
00:11:10,400 --> 00:11:13,380
Brother, you got balls of steel, no joke.

211
00:11:20,160 --> 00:11:20,990
Freezing!

212
00:11:27,440 --> 00:11:28,880
Wowzers! Amazing!

213
00:11:40,800 --> 00:11:42,600
Now aren't you cold?

214
00:11:45,460 --> 00:11:49,740
Oath, sharl, raise,
bend, bard, harp, stools!

215
00:11:53,900 --> 00:11:54,730
Better?

216
00:11:55,000 --> 00:11:57,620
I cast a freeze resistance spell over us.

217
00:12:12,440 --> 00:12:14,400
Tonki! Up here! Yeah!

218
00:12:18,840 --> 00:12:19,670
Jesus!

219
00:12:20,900 --> 00:12:22,120
Take it easy, Klein.

220
00:12:22,380 --> 00:12:24,851
He doesn't look it, but he's a vegetarian.

221
00:12:25,000 --> 00:12:26,340
Well, not exactly.

222
00:12:26,640 --> 00:12:31,522
When I brought him some fish from above
ground, he scarfed it all down in one bite.

223
00:12:32,460 --> 00:12:33,401
What's he doing?

224
00:12:34,720 --> 00:12:37,077
He's telling you to
get on his back is all.

225
00:12:37,160 --> 00:12:39,340
Dude, no way, no way in hell.

226
00:12:39,580 --> 00:12:41,577
My grandpa's dying
words were don't ride in

227
00:12:41,660 --> 00:12:44,137
foreign cars or on
flying Cthulhu elephants.

228
00:12:44,220 --> 00:12:46,517
Is he the same dead grandpa who's dried

229
00:12:46,600 --> 00:12:49,247
figs we were eating at
Dicey's the other day?

230
00:12:49,440 --> 00:12:50,897
Stop farting around and get on it.

231
00:12:50,980 --> 00:12:51,940
It eats me, man.

232
00:12:54,660 --> 00:12:56,000
This is gonna be fun.

233
00:12:56,260 --> 00:12:57,420
We're so dead.

234
00:12:57,800 --> 00:12:59,859
Thanks a lot for doing this, Tonki.

235
00:13:04,860 --> 00:13:05,880
All right, Tonki.

236
00:13:06,440 --> 00:13:09,264
Everyone's on board, so
take us to that dungeon!

237
00:13:22,520 --> 00:13:23,350
Wow.

238
00:13:23,433 --> 00:13:25,757
I wonder what would happen
if you fell from way up here.

239
00:13:25,840 --> 00:13:28,677
The same thing that happened
when a certain someone decided to

240
00:13:28,760 --> 00:13:31,937
get to the next level of Aincrad
by climbing the Outer Pillars.

241
00:13:32,020 --> 00:13:33,357
So how bad at Wonderplutz?

242
00:13:33,440 --> 00:13:34,437
Care to show the lady?

243
00:13:34,520 --> 00:13:35,880
Nah, I think I'll pass.

244
00:13:36,020 --> 00:13:39,517
But maybe one of our more cat-like
friends would like to take a shot.

245
00:13:39,600 --> 00:13:41,306
Nope, nope, nope, nope, nope.

246
00:13:44,660 --> 00:13:45,490
Aaaaaaah!

247
00:13:48,520 --> 00:13:49,350
Aaaaaaah!

248
00:13:50,640 --> 00:13:51,470
Aaaaaaah!

249
00:13:51,860 --> 00:13:52,760
Yee-haw!

250
00:14:04,180 --> 00:14:05,380
Kazuto, get up here!

251
00:14:05,480 --> 00:14:06,310
Check it out!

252
00:14:14,160 --> 00:14:15,037
My god.

253
00:14:15,120 --> 00:14:16,760
I can't believe it.

254
00:14:16,920 --> 00:14:19,757
They figured out how to make
that monster fight for them.

255
00:14:19,840 --> 00:14:21,617
No, there's got to be another reason.

256
00:14:21,700 --> 00:14:24,277
It's not possible to tame
monsters in this game.

257
00:14:24,360 --> 00:14:26,537
Not even if you're a
catsy master tamer with

258
00:14:26,620 --> 00:14:29,032
a full power boost and special equipment.

259
00:14:29,640 --> 00:14:31,777
Then they're leeching off the monster?

260
00:14:31,860 --> 00:14:33,684
No, wait, they're not leeching.

261
00:14:34,100 --> 00:14:34,930
Piggybacking?

262
00:14:35,013 --> 00:14:36,020
Yeah, that's it. See,

263
00:14:36,280 --> 00:14:38,817
that group's got old forearms
there doing all the heavy

264
00:14:38,900 --> 00:14:41,757
lifting and sniping at the
Jelliphant when they get an opening.

265
00:14:41,840 --> 00:14:45,160
But is it that easy to
control a monster's aggro?

266
00:14:45,380 --> 00:14:47,027
It's ignoring everyone else.

267
00:15:06,400 --> 00:15:08,817
How come they're not taking
on that forearm, dude?

268
00:15:08,900 --> 00:15:10,253
Where's everyone going?

269
00:15:10,860 --> 00:15:12,080
Hey, you guys, look!

270
00:15:14,680 --> 00:15:17,520
What the hell's going on down there?

271
00:15:17,800 --> 00:15:22,117
After what we just saw and how it went down,
it should be pretty obvious what it is.

272
00:15:22,200 --> 00:15:26,297
I hate to say it, but we're looking at
that kill quest Asuna told us about.

273
00:15:26,380 --> 00:15:27,777
Even though it's a quest,

274
00:15:27,860 --> 00:15:31,860
helping these forearmed freaks
murder Tonki's friends is disgusting.

275
00:15:39,840 --> 00:15:41,220
Damn, she's tall.

276
00:15:43,780 --> 00:15:46,720
Greetings, I am Urt, Queen of the Lake!

277
00:15:47,720 --> 00:15:50,917
You have bonded with my
kinsmen and I am grateful.

278
00:15:51,000 --> 00:15:54,277
My two younger sisters and
I have spoken at length.

279
00:15:54,360 --> 00:15:56,377
And we have a request for you.

280
00:15:56,460 --> 00:16:01,937
If you would be so kind, we ask that you
save our lands from the Frost Giants?

281
00:16:02,020 --> 00:16:03,000
Daddy!

282
00:16:04,100 --> 00:16:05,357
She's an NPC.

283
00:16:05,440 --> 00:16:08,028
There's something strange
about her, though.

284
00:16:08,220 --> 00:16:10,757
Her speech pattern doesn't
follow the same set

285
00:16:10,840 --> 00:16:13,440
response routines that
a normal NPC's would.

286
00:16:13,940 --> 00:16:18,411
Her core programming is connected to
the language engine module of the game.

287
00:16:18,700 --> 00:16:19,757
What are you saying?

288
00:16:19,840 --> 00:16:21,200
Is she some kind of AI?

289
00:16:21,560 --> 00:16:23,120
Yes, Daddy, she is.

290
00:16:23,380 --> 00:16:26,937
In the past, Jotunheim was
similar to your Alfheim.

291
00:16:27,020 --> 00:16:30,120
Covered in lush greenery
and beautiful lakes,

292
00:16:30,380 --> 00:16:33,900
it basked in the blessings
of Yggdrasil, the world tree.

293
00:16:35,360 --> 00:16:40,940
We, the hill giants, lived in peace and
harmony with our kinfolk, the creatures.

294
00:16:42,760 --> 00:16:48,660
Far below the splendor of Jotunheim is a
realm of ice and snow known as Niflheim.

295
00:16:49,240 --> 00:16:52,557
Thrimmer, king of the frost
giants, rules that land.

296
00:16:52,640 --> 00:16:56,160
He shattered our peace
by casting Excalibur,

297
00:16:56,280 --> 00:16:58,751
the sword that slices through wooden iron,

298
00:16:59,040 --> 00:17:02,600
into the well of Oort,
the heart of our land.

299
00:17:03,780 --> 00:17:07,080
It severed the thickest
roots of the world tree.

300
00:17:07,560 --> 00:17:12,320
In an instant, Jotunheim lost the
blessings it received from Yggdrasil.

301
00:17:30,820 --> 00:17:33,620
I was right, Excalibur.

302
00:17:35,320 --> 00:17:37,080
Under Thrymmer's command,

303
00:17:37,380 --> 00:17:41,540
the Frost Giants marched on Jotunheim
and overwhelmed our defenses.

304
00:17:42,020 --> 00:17:45,080
Their fortresses and castles
soon blighted our land,

305
00:17:45,240 --> 00:17:48,660
and scores of my people were
captured and imprisoned.

306
00:17:49,260 --> 00:17:52,380
Once they seized control,
they built Thrymheim.

307
00:17:52,640 --> 00:17:57,580
Their largest castle, atop the mass
of ice once known as the Well of Oort.

308
00:17:58,760 --> 00:18:03,460
During the chaos, my sisters and I
escaped to the bottom of a frozen lake.

309
00:18:03,920 --> 00:18:06,940
However, we no longer have
the power we once had.

310
00:18:07,940 --> 00:18:11,540
The frost giants are not
satisfied with their spoils.

311
00:18:11,780 --> 00:18:16,600
They wish to annihilate our kin, the
creatures that populate our realm.

312
00:18:18,420 --> 00:18:19,660
If they succeed,

313
00:18:19,980 --> 00:18:24,600
my powers will be extinguished, and
Thrymheim will rise to the next world,

314
00:18:24,880 --> 00:18:26,700
your world, Alfheim.

315
00:18:27,940 --> 00:18:28,960
Hold the phone!

316
00:18:29,180 --> 00:18:30,997
You're telling us that
once they're done here,

317
00:18:31,080 --> 00:18:32,977
they're going to go up and destroy Arun?

318
00:18:33,060 --> 00:18:34,780
Yes, that is their intention.

319
00:18:35,500 --> 00:18:37,937
King Thrymmer will seal Alfheim in ice and

320
00:18:38,020 --> 00:18:41,480
continue on until he reaches
the top of Yggdrasil.

321
00:18:43,400 --> 00:18:47,500
Once he reaches it, he will take
the golden apple growing there.

322
00:18:49,240 --> 00:18:51,557
Thrimmer and his generals
have grown frustrated

323
00:18:51,640 --> 00:18:54,317
by the time it is taking
to wipe out my kinfolk,

324
00:18:54,400 --> 00:18:56,157
so they have turned to your people,

325
00:18:56,240 --> 00:18:59,380
the fairies, for assistance
in their murderous plot.

326
00:18:59,880 --> 00:19:02,500
Your kind hunts our kinfolk to extinction,

327
00:19:02,900 --> 00:19:05,680
lured by the offer of
Excalibur as a reward.

328
00:19:08,760 --> 00:19:12,380
However, King Thrymmer cannot
bestow that sword onto others.

329
00:19:13,020 --> 00:19:15,820
For if Excalibur ever leaves Thrymheim,

330
00:19:16,120 --> 00:19:19,179
the blessings of Yggdrasil
will return to this land,

331
00:19:19,300 --> 00:19:22,840
and their castle will vanish
as a mist upon a meadow.

332
00:19:23,160 --> 00:19:28,180
But then, what kind of quest is it
when the reward forward is a total lie?

333
00:19:28,400 --> 00:19:30,518
How is he going to get away with it?

334
00:19:30,660 --> 00:19:31,490
Most likely,

335
00:19:31,573 --> 00:19:33,937
he will award the victor
a sword called Caliburn,

336
00:19:34,020 --> 00:19:36,740
whose appearance is
identical to Excalibur.

337
00:19:36,960 --> 00:19:38,136
But that's cheating!

338
00:19:38,320 --> 00:19:40,977
If he's a king, doesn't
he have a code of honor?

339
00:19:41,060 --> 00:19:45,472
Unfortunately, cheating and falsehoods
are Thrimmer's most powerful assets.

340
00:19:46,020 --> 00:19:49,140
However, he has made one great mistake.

341
00:19:50,200 --> 00:19:52,540
In his eagerness to slaughter my kin,

342
00:19:52,840 --> 00:19:55,117
he has sent a number
of his giants down from

343
00:19:55,200 --> 00:19:57,720
Thrymheim to marshal your kind for battle.

344
00:19:58,520 --> 00:20:02,957
At this moment, the defenses of his castle
are weaker than they have ever been.

345
00:20:03,040 --> 00:20:04,040
There's our shot.

346
00:20:11,440 --> 00:20:14,357
Once the stone in the amulet turns black,

347
00:20:14,440 --> 00:20:19,840
it will mean all my kinfolk have been
slain, and my powers have left me.

348
00:20:20,900 --> 00:20:23,800
Good fairies, infiltrate Thrymheim,

349
00:20:24,100 --> 00:20:27,420
remove Excalibur from its
plinth, and save my realm.

350
00:20:31,980 --> 00:20:34,520
I am counting on you, good fairies.

351
00:20:41,900 --> 00:20:44,900
This is turning into a
bigger deal than we thought.

352
00:20:45,180 --> 00:20:47,460
Is this still considered a quest?

353
00:20:47,680 --> 00:20:49,197
Because it's kind of...

354
00:20:49,280 --> 00:20:52,751
turned into something way more
epic than a plain old quest.

355
00:20:53,000 --> 00:20:53,940
You heard her.

356
00:20:54,200 --> 00:20:56,817
She said if the creatures in
this world get killed off,

357
00:20:56,900 --> 00:21:00,780
The Frost Giants will take over
the surface next. Yeah, I know.

358
00:21:01,220 --> 00:21:03,477
But I doubt the Admins
would let that happen

359
00:21:03,560 --> 00:21:06,619
without some kind of update
or warning or something.

360
00:21:07,060 --> 00:21:11,060
I mean, normally, they'd let
players know a week ahead of time.

361
00:21:12,520 --> 00:21:13,350
Whatever.

362
00:21:13,433 --> 00:21:16,315
We're gonna finish this quest
for Tonki, right, Kazuto?

363
00:21:16,560 --> 00:21:17,460
You know it.

364
00:21:17,680 --> 00:21:20,777
We were gonna storm the castle
and grab Excalibur anyway.

365
00:21:20,860 --> 00:21:23,684
It'll be easy if the
castle's defenses are down.

366
00:21:23,820 --> 00:21:26,761
Helping Tonki and his
friends out, that's a bonus.

367
00:21:29,900 --> 00:21:32,782
Here we go, guys, our last
big quest of the year.

368
00:21:32,940 --> 00:21:37,411
Let's bank this thing and score us a
spot on the front page of MMO tomorrow.

369
00:21:37,920 --> 00:21:38,750
Yeah!

370
00:21:45,200 --> 00:21:46,553
Don't you worry, Tonki.

371
00:21:46,800 --> 00:21:48,637
We'll get your home back for you.

372
00:21:48,720 --> 00:21:50,485
It'll be good as new, promise.

373
00:21:58,500 --> 00:22:00,460
Here we go!

374
00:22:04,600 --> 00:22:07,240
Unique Loverty

375
00:22:13,260 --> 00:22:17,337
I'm on my own face.

376
00:22:17,420 --> 00:22:19,097
I'm on my own face.

377
00:22:19,180 --> 00:22:25,720
And all of you talk to me?

378
00:22:27,380 --> 00:22:30,200
Hey, TV no na ka?

379
00:22:30,720 --> 00:22:35,877
Hero ga mi lai no tame ni!

380
00:22:35,960 --> 00:22:39,137
Iso ga shi soo!

381
00:22:39,220 --> 00:22:42,297
Hoka ni wa nai.

382
00:22:42,380 --> 00:22:46,140
Bi gokoji ga alu yo.

383
00:22:46,720 --> 00:22:49,157
My room now.

384
00:22:49,240 --> 00:22:53,557
Hitori ga Sugou Daddy no ni?

385
00:22:53,640 --> 00:22:59,300
What are You Thanks?

386
00:22:59,940 --> 00:23:00,770
Is You What Are Your Mother?

387
00:23:00,853 --> 00:23:01,683
Are You In My Friends?

388
00:23:01,940 --> 00:23:04,520
Is You What Are You?

389
00:23:05,300 --> 00:23:09,717
Am I In

390
00:23:09,800 --> 00:23:12,477
My Friends?

391
00:23:12,560 --> 00:23:15,260
Are You In My Friends?

392
00:23:15,700 --> 00:23:18,577
Here I am I'll

393
00:23:18,660 --> 00:23:22,977
see you

394
00:23:23,060 --> 00:23:30,060
next

395
00:23:35,520 --> 00:23:36,740
time,

396
00:23:36,980 --> 00:23:38,333
the King of the Giants.
